WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
Right now, your cells are pumping
ions across their membranes,

2
00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:05.630
against the gradient.

3
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.180
That takes energy.

4
00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:10.630
And in the end, your cells
get their energy from sugar.

5
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.910
Yet the pump doesn't run on sugar.

6
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.300
It runs on a different molecule: ATP.

7
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.290
Why would a cell spend its
energy through a go-between,

8
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.690
instead of spending sugar directly?

9
00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:26.910
In this mission, you'll split ATP with
water and watch energy being released.

10
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.480
Then you'll see how that release is
linked to work the cell needs done.

11
00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:36.910
Your mission: find out why cells spend
sugar's energy through ATP first.
